.TH EARSHOT 1 "November 2026" "earshot 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
earshot \- local speech-to-text with whisper.cpp
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B earshot
[OPTIONS] FILE...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B earshot
transcribes audio locally. It supports CPU and CUDA backends, automatic language
detection, optional Silero voice activity detection, and TXT, SRT, WebVTT and
JSON output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.B earshot -l en lesson.mp3
.br
.B earshot --format srt,vtt -o subtitles lesson.m4a
.br
.B earshot --device cpu -m small.en interview.wav
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-m, --model " NAME
Whisper model name or path to a GGML model. Defaults to large-v3-turbo.
.TP
.BI "-l, --language " LANG
Spoken language code, or auto for detection.
.TP
.B --translate
Translate the speech to English instead of transcribing it verbatim.
.TP
.B --no-vad
Disable voice activity detection.
.TP
.BI "-o, --output " PATH
Output file or directory. The default is next to the input file.
.TP
.BI "--format " LIST
Comma-separated txt, srt, vtt or json formats.
.TP
.B -p, --paragraphs
Group text output into readable paragraphs.
.TP
.B --device auto|cpu|cuda
Select the inference backend.
.TP
.B --force
Overwrite existing output files.
.TP
.B --help
Show the complete option list.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/earshot/models
Downloaded model weights, unless XDG_CACHE_HOME or --models-dir is used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH AUTHOR
BradAkemi
